WEBVTT

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.990
"Life Lessons with Uramichi Oniisan"

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.080
Episode 12: Awkward Smile

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.380
So sleepy.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.460
Hm?

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:51.670
Oh, I see... That's what's happening, huh?

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.130
Yes.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.140
To be honest, I feel like
I've reached my limits.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.390
Then you'll really...

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.060
Yeah.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.850
I'll quit at the end of this month.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.980
I guess it can't be helped.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.110
But I'm sure that you'll be able
to find the best place for you.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.900
I'll be rooting for you.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.700
Thank you very much.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.040
What...? Quit...? Is he serious?!

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.620
Uramichi-<i>san</i>...!

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.210
What?

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.590
Maybe you're mistaken?

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:34.130
No, I'm not! He looked very serious, too.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.430
He's gonna quit being a
gymnast Oniisan. I'm sure of it!

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:46.770
I was so surprised that
I thought maybe I was dreaming.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.770
I'm not sure...

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:52.110
...but he doesn't look like someone
who'd quit his job so easily.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.990
Hey! You jerk! Don't eat just
the peanuts in the <i>kaki-pi</i>!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.790
I'm gonna miss him if he quits.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.340
Yeah... we've known each other
for such a long time.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.000
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.130
Don't quit!

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:17.550
Who are you shouting at?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:23.680
Anyway, the way you guys and Uramichi-<i>san</i>
met was really fateful, wasn't it?

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.430
Yeah. It brings back memories.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.850
If it wasn't for that coincidence...

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.860
...we definitely wouldn't...

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:35.900
"Congrats"
"All Japan Male Gymnastics Meet"
"First Place, Uramichi Omota"
"Second Place, Volleyball Team"

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.620
Seriously, please! This is
the last favor I'll ask of you!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.960
I heard that they got cute girls
for today's group date.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.840
Just the first party would do!
I'll treat you to a meal. So, please?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.380
"First Place, Uramichi Omota"
"Second Place, Volleyball Team"

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.880
You should hang out
with friends for a change,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.890
instead of just studying and
practicing Japanese archery.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.350
It's none of your business.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.810
Okay, then! Meet me at eight
in front of the station!

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.350
What? Hey!

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.770
That jerk...

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.770
Hm?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.610
Excuse me. You dropped your handkerchief.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.610
What?

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.820
Oh, thank you.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.110
Here you go.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:23.200
Um... What time is it?

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.950
What? Oh... it's 1:22.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.790
Thank you very much! Well then!

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.630
But he was wearing a watch...

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.960
What a weird guy.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.510
Hey, hey. What do you do for fun?

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.140
Well... Watch movies, I guess?

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:45.680
What, seriously?! I love movies, too!

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.140
Really? Have you watched
anything you liked recently?

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.140
Er... Let's see... there're just so many.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.110
Oh, that one! I liked that one.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.100
Tobikichi Usahara

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:58.400
<i>Red Flamingos</i>! Oh, and<i> One Flew Over</i>
<i>the Bull-headed Strike's Nest</i>!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:00.110
Are you a model by
any chance? You're so cute.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.110
They're pretty basic, though.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.820
What? What do you mean? Stop it.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:04.070
What? What did you say?
Um... Oh, yeah. I know them.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.070
Really, you're so cute!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.750
Let's see. It's that one, right?
A guy and a woman appear.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:09.830
Mitsuo Kumatani

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.750
You look super cute with that hairstyle.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:09.490
Excuse me.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.290
Hm?

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:14.710
Do you not like group dates
that much, Kumatani-<i>san</i>?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.210
What?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.800
Oh, I rarely participate in them at all,
and I don't really like them, either.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.180
If you like, can we go
somewhere alone after this?

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.050
Well, I've got classes tomorrow,
so I'm going home now.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.930
What? Ah...

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.520
Thanks, guys.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:31.390
What?! Hey! Are you going home, Kumatani?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.850
Sorry, guys! I have to take
care of something, too!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.610
--What?
--You're already leaving?
--Such a party pooper.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:42.650
Ahh... I wanna be funny.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.410
I wonder what kinds of
topics cute girls like.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.450
I seriously don't understand.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.960
It backfired on you because
you started talking about movies

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.580
when you don't know anything about them.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.420
You've never even been able to
sit still and watch for two hours.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.550
Kumatani. Have you finished
the homework for Sports Research?

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:03.340
What? It's due tomorrow.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.050
Hey! Let me see yours!
This is the last favor I'll ask of you!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.510
How many "last favors"
are you going to ask for?

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.600
Oh, stop sweating the small stuff.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.100
Hey, please!

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.020
Don't just say whatever's
most convenient for you.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.480
Please! Kumatani-<i>kun</i>!

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.560
You're being creepy.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.480
Don't be so coldhearted.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.610
At any rate, Nekota is acting
like a stranger, leaving the dorm

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.110
because he's going to
live with his girlfriend.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.530
I wish I could say something like that.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.280
Let's keep moving!
Twenty-four hours of music!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:32.330
It's so annoying to live alone with you.
I hope someone moves in soon.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.410
<i>Nagara TV</i>! The new segment is
"Listen to this if you have time!! 500 songs."

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.410
That's mean.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:37.830
This is Oricon rank 499, "Matching Look
of Love in Naniwa" by Yasuko Oide!

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.830
Oh, yeah. Did you see
that banner hanging at school?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.670
Yeah, I did.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.670
Here we go!

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.380
Isn't Uramichi Omota amazing?

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:45.430
♬ ...double-stacked and pink color contacts ♬

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:45.430
I don't know much about gymnastics,
but I can just tell he's really amazing.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.680
You really don't know anything.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:50.600
♬ The <i>takoyaki </i>we ate in the mall food court ♬

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.600
You know, I saw him
in the cafeteria the other--

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.850
Hm? Who could that be this late at night?

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.140
Coming!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.690
Oh, it's you, Dorm Caretaker.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.940
I'm sorry to come by so late at night.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.900
I know this is short notice,

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.490
but the renovation of the east dorm
building will start tomorrow.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:12.330
Since you have a vacancy, I'd like you
to let someone stay for the time being.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.000
Oh, no problem.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.290
He's not a freshman like you,
but please make him feel welcome.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.210
Whoa!

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:24.840
I'm Uramichi Omota.
I'm from the east building.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.430
Nice to meet you.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.600
Uramichi-<i>san</i>. You're stupid, idiot!

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:42.110
Hurry and get up.
Or I'll leave you here and go home.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.280
I've always admired him.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.200
I might throw up.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.030
Whoa!

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.530
What?! What'd you do that for?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.120
Whoa! Oops!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.920
Hey... What do you think I should do?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.590
About what?

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:10.640
Ever since my college days,
I've always admired Uramichi-<i>san</i>.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.060
While there are times I get nervous,
working at the same place,

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:19.060
when all is said and done, I do have fun.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.850
Yeah.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:27.110
I know that Uramichi-<i>san </i>is really clumsy
with everything except for gymnastics.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.780
You'll get beat up if you tell him that.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:33.830
No, it's not like that.
I'm not making fun of him.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:37.160
Gymnastics is all he's ever had.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.710
One last time!

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:48.760
Ow...!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.180
Tobikichi-<i>kun</i>! Are you okay?!

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.890
Ow...

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.770
I twisted my ankle a little.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:02.310
Oh, no, you've done it. Do you
wanna go to the medical office?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.730
No, I'm okay. I'll use ice.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.150
Okay. I'll get you a bag.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.900
Thanks so much!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.950
The first summer
after I started college...

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.370
Hm?

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.120
Whoa! That's a lot of rain clouds!

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:23.830
Although I live with the school's star,
we haven't opened up with each other yet.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.460
Tobikichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.880
And I heard that the east building's
renovation will be over soon.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.880
Yeah.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.890
By the way, Tobikichi-<i>kun</i>,

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:37.680
is it true that you live in the same
dorm room as Uramichi Omota?

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.520
Yeah. Isn't that cool?

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.730
Sounds nice. Introduce him to me!

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:43.270
What? Why?

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:44.980
Because he's cool, right?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.820
Maybe I should've become a gymnastics
team manager instead of track and field.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.570
What? Someone like that is your type?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.620
Yeah, kinda... Hey, ask him
if he's got a girlfriend.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.370
He does! He probably does!

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.830
No, he definitely does!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:09.000
Um... Do you... have a girlfriend?

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.210
I don't.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:14.680
Oh, crap...

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:19.010
The giant typhoon that formed
the other day is fast approaching Japan

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:23.930
Reporter

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:23.930
Riko Doshabu

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:24.850
and is bringing heavy rain,
while the wind is still getting stronger!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.940
Doshabu-<i>san</i>? Doshabu-<i>san</i>?!

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:31.110
Everyone, please be careful
and stay inside as much as possible.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.030
It looks like it's getting crazy outside.

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.610
Yeah.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:40.080
I wonder if there are really people
who'd go outside in this weather.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.540
There are...!

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.880
What?! What happened?
Did something explode?!

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:48.590
I'll go check it out.

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:49.670
Ah!

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.500
I'll come with--

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.960
Ow!

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:58.850
Ah... I'll be right behind you,
so please go ahead.

00:10:58.850 --> 00:10:59.970
Okay.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.350
Whoa...

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.060
This is the sacred tree
that was behind the building.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.690
Do sacred trees normally come down?

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:13.530
It was good that no one was in the
building because of the renovation.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.570
There would've been casualties otherwise.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.570
Yeah, it could've been worse.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.790
So, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>. About your dorm room...

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:27.620
Was it just a natural disaster...
or an act of God...?

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:31.130
And so, the dorm that our college star
was supposed to go back to was crushed,

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:35.300
and we started fully living together with
him, the star who was going to graduate

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:39.510
before the building repair
would be complete.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.770
Um... Usa... Usa...

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.730
What? Oh, me?

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.690
The name is Usahara. Tobikichi Usahara.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.320
Usahara. Is your foot okay?

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.870
Ahh... I twisted my ankle a little
while practicing today.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:05.200
I used ice, but it's
started to get swollen.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.250
Let me see.

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:08.000
What?! Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait...

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.710
It's not your bone. I wonder
if you hurt a ligament.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.630
Why didn't you go
to a hospital right away?

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:17.550
Well... I can still walk,
so it's not a big deal.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:18.800
Hm?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.300
Aren't you scared?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.310
This could end everything for you.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.230
What? Well, you're making
a big deal out of it.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:33.060
Even if I couldn't do
field and track anymore...

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.690
He wasn't scolding me
or trying to reason with me.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:41.360
How should I react to his pure,
questioning eyes, just like a child's?

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.490
Go to a hospital tomorrow.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.790
The doctors there take
good care of their patients.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.740
"Orthopedic and Sports"
"Ashi Clinic"

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:52.000
Okay.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.500
By the way, did you see Kumatani around?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.010
I wonder where he went.

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:04.220
Okay, you guys can go in.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:09.270
That's a pretty good covering
from the rain, isn't it?

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:16.020
Orthopedic and Sports - Ashi Clinic

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:15.980
Please take care.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.320
Hmm...

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.990
I've never used a crutch.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.620
I'm Yasuko Oide!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.460
Hm?

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.710
I'll sing with all my heart.
Please listen.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.920
"Yasuko Oide"

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:38.550
The song is "Matching Look
of Love in Naniwa."

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:44.220
♬ You and I in acrylic knits ♬

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.510
I can't get used to the crutch.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.020
Whoa!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.310
Are you okay?

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.480
Please be careful.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.400
What a super good-looking high-schooler...

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:03.200
I bet he's popular with girls.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:05.200
I guess I'll go to school for now.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.870
Ah! Isn't that Tobikichi-<i>kun</i>?!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.630
G'morning, Tobikichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.840
Oh, you're using a crutch.
Oh, shoot! Are you okay?

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.670
It's not a big deal, but I was
told to use it just in case.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:25.760
Jeez... You should've gone
to the medical office right away.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.010
I know, right?

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.760
Ah! Uramichi Omota.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.890
What? Where? Where?

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.430
Ah! You're right!

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.560
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.350
I went to the clinic you recommended!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:41.650
It's all good. Thank you very--
Oops. That was close.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.030
This could end everything for you.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.110
Are you okay? Be careful!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:53.830
Those words somehow weighed on my mind,
and I kept thinking back on them.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.880
Gymnastics may be all he's got...

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:01.550
I thought so when I saw his awkward smile.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.050
Okay!

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.590
Well, going on and on about it
won't get me anywhere!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.260
Let's casually ask Uramichi-<i>san</i>
about it tomorrow!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.060
Okay, Kumatani?!

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:13.730
Why involve me?

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:17.730
That's... because I'm scared, of course.

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:20.270
How weakhearted.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:24.900
Gymnastics is all Uramichi-<i>san</i>'s ever had.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:34.250
That's true... But to me,
that side of him was...

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.380
Ahh, it was so heavy!

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:45.010
College life goes by so quickly.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.720
What's with that <i>kotatsu</i>? What happened?

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:52.760
Well, my mom told me to take it with me
in order to save on the shipping fee.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.480
I wonder if Uramichi-<i>san </i>is back yet.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.690
Today is the last day of the winter break.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:00.560
I wonder where his parents live.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.020
Hm? What?

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.820
Well... your dialect...

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.860
Oh... It comes back whenever I go home.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.620
People tend to have a bias just because
a person is from Kyoto, right?

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:13.080
But I'm definitely not two-faced, okay?

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:16.450
Yeah, that shows... in a bad way.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.790
In a bad way?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.620
Hm?

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:20.880
Happy New Year.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:24.050
Oh, it's you, Nekota. Someone with
a girlfriend should go home.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.920
Oh, don't say that.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:29.510
I feel lonely since she
isn't back from her parents'.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.340
I brought this, so...

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:32.760
Oh, thank you!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.930
Ah! Is that a <i>kotatsu</i>?

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.230
The heater doesn't work well,

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:40.650
so my mom told me to take
their old <i>kotatsu </i>with me.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:42.690
Nice. Let's assemble it.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.280
I like the <i>kotatsu </i>better
than the heater, anyway.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:49.360
You're gonna stay here
for a while, aren't you?

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.740
Oh? Where're you going?

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.120
I'm gonna go get coffee.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.280
Oh, I want cocoa.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.370
I want plum kelp tea.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:55.370
Okay.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:06.210
Ah... Kuma... Kuma...

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.630
It's Kumatani.

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:08.970
Kumatani.

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:11.510
You've already started training?

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:14.430
Ah... Yeah.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:17.680
By any chance have you been
doing it alone during the break?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:18.890
Sorta...

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.810
You didn't go home?

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.310
Kinda...

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.020
What's with this guy?

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:29.320
Usahara and others talk like
he's a superstar, but I feel a little...

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.910
...no, rather, really
uncomfortable around him.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:37.120
When I was small, although
I was only a child, I thought

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:41.540
that lies and laziness were
truly characteristics of humans.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.740
Boy Mitsuo (5 years old)

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.960
My grandad was a fisherman.
My dad was a chef.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:47.000
Maybe because they had an artisan spirit,

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.760
but my family was increasingly
becoming stricter every year.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:53.840
I rebelled against it...
and became a delinquent.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.920
Boy Mitsuo (15 years old)

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.010
'Sup!

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:59.310
Don't become crooked.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.310
'Sup, Kumatani-<i>san</i>!

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:03.140
Youngsters must work hard and
devote themselves to something.

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:00.730
Shut up.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:03.140
Sorry!

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:06.060
I really hated those expectations
that people had.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.570
Mitsuo! You lazy dog!

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.990
How dare you get your mom
called in by your school!

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:13.490
I'm fine. Please stop, honey.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:17.410
As was expected, my relationship
with my family was the worst then.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.580
Hey, you're back! Let's play a game!

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:21.540
Sure!

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:24.290
But my little brother was
an exception. We were close.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:32.300
Because of his casual suggestion, I joined
the Japanese archery club in high school.

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:35.800
Eventually, I stopped fighting
and plainly disobeying my parents.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.390
Brother!

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:40.310
You should join a club. I'll join one
after starting middle school, too.

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:41.180
Which club?

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.140
I'll draw lots to decide.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:48.190
I thought that I'd be able to understand
what it meant to live stoically

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.860
if I got immersed in sports and such.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:53.150
But my revulsion towards it
was still present.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:57.490
"Inbox"
"Usahara" "No subject"
"Usahara" "No subject"
"Usahara" "No subject"

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.820
"Buy some ingredients for
hot pot dish while you're out"

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.700
That jerk...

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.210
Uramichi-<i>san</i>. I'm going to a supermarket.
What're you gonna do?

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:05.420
What?

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:08.750
That sounded like I was
inviting him to come with me.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.670
Ah... well... Please go back to the dorm.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.130
I'll go with you.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.380
What?

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:23.680
What do you usually do to relax?

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.480
Relax?

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:29.730
Ah... Never mind. Don't you get tired
being so serious all the time?

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.900
I'm not really serious.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.450
Being serious doesn't mean just
doing the things you're told, right?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.210
Hm?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.340
I'm sorry.

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.670
No problem.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.510
Thank you very much.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:56.010
We should name her right away
when we get home.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.340
Yeah.

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.810
I thought that you were the serious type.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:05.480
You submit reports, so...

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:08.140
I just don't want people
to think I slack off.

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:11.900
I think he was probably feeling lonely
being by himself during the winter break.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:10.440
Isn't that just called "being serious"?

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:12.770
I think it'll be lively when we get back.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:14.610
That might be why
he came along to go shopping.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.610
Oh, okay.

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.070
I guess.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:21.200
Hey, what took you so long,
Kumatani? I'm hungry.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.410
Shut up.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.950
Ah! Uramichi-<i>san</i>! Happy New Year!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.830
What?! Uramichi Omota?!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.750
The hot pot dish Kumatani
makes is really good.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.460
This week's single rank 498.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.750
I'm making it again?

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.380
"Ame-Mura, My Love," by Yasuko Oide.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:35.380
Please make your
restaurant-trained hot pot dish.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.970
Help me a little! Don't loaf around!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:39.550
What?

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.720
More importantly,
did you finish your report?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.850
Don't talk about it, please.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:51.980
Present Time

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.270
It hurts...

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:50.060
My head hurts.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.270
I had too much to drink yesterday.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.020
Good morning!

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.820
Good morning!

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:59.570
Uramichi-<i>san</i>! Good morning.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.860
Yeah.

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.410
What's wrong? You look pale.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:05.740
What? Oh, I do?

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:07.830
I bet you had too much to drink, right?

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.330
What...? Well...

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.420
Here. I'll give you some
medicine for your stomach.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:15.420
Thank you very much.
You're being kind for some reason.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.590
Really? This is normal.

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:20.430
What is it? Did something good happen?

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.470
Hmm... Something like that.

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:24.930
I found a good place.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.510
A good place?

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.100
Yeah, it's the best place to be.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.480
Well, good luck with the shoot today.

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:39.280
Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:42.410
Are you... happy like that?

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:46.870
Well... I guess I am.

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:55.420
Morning!

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:56.960
Good morning.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.590
What's the matter? Why are you in a daze?

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:01.970
Are you hungry?

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:06.100
I can't stop him.

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:07.140
Hm?

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:10.640
Uramichi-<i>san </i>wants to quit his job.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.190
What?
